Recommendation for Future Documentation
To avoid losing these essential instructions again, I recommend two things for your next project:

Create a README.md File: In your new GitHub repository (atlas-series-final-launch), create a file named README.md. Copy all the instructions from the table above into this file. This makes the documentation live alongside the code.

Use Simple Comments: When you make future code edits, leave a brief HTML comment (<!-- YOUR COMMENT HERE -->) right next to the code explaining why you made the change.

By documenting your setup within the new repository, you ensure the "tutorials" are always exactly where you need them!







